tasks.description:
CREATE ONE NEW FILE: scripts/scs001/validate-phase1-activation.ts. Do NOT modify any existing file.

This script validates whether the system is correctly configured for Phase 1 live TikTok posting. It does NOT make any API calls and does NOT post to TikTok. It reads config files and environment state, then writes a readiness report.

EXACT REQUIREMENTS:

1. IMPORTS:
   import { readFileSync, writeFileSync, mkdirSync, existsSync } from 'fs';
   import { join } from 'path';
   No other imports.

2. DEFINE these interfaces inline:
   interface ReadinessCheck { id: string; name: string; pass: boolean; details: string; action_required?: string; }
   interface ReadinessReport { sprint: string; date: string; phase: string; checks: ReadinessCheck[]; ready_to_post: boolean; human_actions_required: string[]; notes: string; }

3. CHECK 1 — ecosystem.config.js has scs001-live process (id: 'ecosystem-live-process', name: 'ecosystem.config.js has scs001-live process'):
   a. Read join(process.cwd(), 'ecosystem.config.js') as a string.
   b. pass = content.includes('"scs001-live"') || content.includes("'scs001-live'");
   c. details = pass ? 'scs001-live process found in ecosystem.config.js' : 'scs001-live process NOT found in ecosystem.config.js';
   d. action_required (only if not pass) = 'Add scs001-live process to ecosystem.config.js';

4. CHECK 2 — TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN env var is set (id: 'tiktok-token', name: 'TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN env var present'):
   a. const token = process.env.TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN || '';
   b. pass = token.length > 0;
   c. details = pass ? 'TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN is set (length: ' + token.length + ' chars)' : 'TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN is NOT set in environment';
   d. action_required (only if not pass) = 'Set TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN in .env — obtain from TikTok Developer Portal, video.upload scope required';

5. CHECK 3 — TikTok client config file exists (id: 'tiktok-client-config', name: 'TikTok client config exists'):
   a. const configPath = join(process.cwd(), 'agents', 'tiktok-client', 'config.ts');
   b. pass = existsSync(configPath);
   c. details = pass ? 'agents/tiktok-client/config.ts exists' : 'agents/tiktok-client/config.ts NOT found';
   d. action_required (only if not pass) = 'TikTok client config is missing — check agents/tiktok-client/';

6. CHECK 4 — scs001-pipeline mock process still present (id: 'mock-fallback', name: 'Mock pipeline fallback preserved'):
   a. Reuse the ecosystem.config.js content from Check 1.
   b. pass = content.includes('"scs001-pipeline"') || content.includes("'scs001-pipeline'");
   c. details = pass ? 'scs001-pipeline mock process still present — dry-run fallback intact' : 'WARNING: scs001-pipeline mock process was removed';
   (No action_required for this check — it is informational.)

7. BUILD ReadinessReport:
   const checks = [check1, check2, check3, check4];
   const criticalChecks = [check1, check2, check3];
   const ready_to_post = criticalChecks.every(c => c.pass);
   const human_actions_required = checks.filter(c => c.action_required).map(c => c.action_required as string);
   const notes = ready_to_post
     ? 'System configured for Phase 1 live posting. Run: pm2 start ecosystem.config.js --only scs001-live'
     : 'System NOT ready for live posting. Complete all human actions above before starting scs001-live.';
   const report: ReadinessReport = { sprint: '097', date: new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10), phase: 'phase-1-activation', checks, ready_to_post, human_actions_required, notes };

8. WRITE report:
   const gatesDir = join(process.cwd(), 'workspace', 'gates');
   mkdirSync(gatesDir, { recursive: true });
   writeFileSync(join(gatesDir, 'phase1-activation-readiness.json'), JSON.stringify(report, null, 2));

9. PRINT results:
   checks.forEach(c => console.log((c.pass ? '\u2713' : '\u2717') + ' [' + c.name + ']: ' + c.details));
   if (human_actions_required.length > 0) { console.log(''); console.log('HUMAN ACTIONS REQUIRED:'); human_actions_required.forEach((a, i) => console.log('  ' + (i + 1) + '. ' + a)); }
   console.log('');
   console.log(ready_to_post ? 'PHASE 1 READY' : 'PHASE 1 BLOCKED — complete actions above');
   console.log('Report written to workspace/gates/phase1-activation-readiness.json');

10. EXIT: process.exit(ready_to_post ? 0 : 1);

11. STRUCTURE: wrap all in async function main(): Promise<void> {} and call main().catch(err => { console.error(err); process.exit(1); });

FAIL CONDITIONS:
(1) Any import other than 'fs' and 'path'
(2) File not created
(3) workspace/gates/phase1-activation-readiness.json not written
(4) ready_to_post field missing from JSON
(5) TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN check does not use process.env directly
(6) process.exit not called
(7) Any existing file modified
